 "equipment_type": "Packaged rooftop unit / DOAS controller",
 "applies_to": "Reznor MAPS III and MAPS IV modular air processing units (packaged DX rooftop units for high outside air) with control option D19.",
 "summary": "MAPS III and MAPS IV units with control option D19 use a programmable system controller with an optional BMS card for BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP/Ethernet. The D19 point list has 29 analog variables, 6 integer variables (AV 1001-1006) and 35 digital variables. The BMS can enable the unit, write discharge air, damper, economizer, pressure and CO2 setpoints and share outdoor temperature and humidity; it reads temperatures, mode flags, compressor and heat stage commands, fan, filter, safety and phase status.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 77000,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The point list is the CP-MAPSIII-D19 form (Doc No 303069) reprinted inside the combined MAPS III/IV controls guide (06-26).",
  "Analog variables are AV 1-29, integer variables AV 1001-1006 and digital variables BV 1-35.",
  "Building and duct static pressure points (AV 1001-1003, AV 1006) are integers; the guide says to divide them by 1000 in the BMS.",
  "D19 has no occupancy or state select points in BACnet; occupancy comes from the unit's own inputs (BV 11 shows the occupied input).",
  "Source: Option D19 BACnet Point List, guide pages 107-108."
 ],
